Types of Monitoring

🔹 What is it? 📊
 Monitoring is not just one thing—it includes different layers of your system.
 The main types are Infrastructure, Application, and Network monitoring.

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 Modern systems are complex. A failure can happen at any layer.
 👉 You need different types of monitoring to detect issues everywhere.

🔹 Key Types of Monitoring: ⚡
✔ Infrastructure Monitoring 🖥️
Tracks servers, CPU, memory, disk
Focus: System health
✔ Application Monitoring 🚀
Tracks app performance
Response time, errors, requests
✔ Network Monitoring 🌐
Tracks network traffic
Latency, packet loss, connectivity

🔹 Real-world Examples: 💡
👉 Infrastructure Issue
CPU usage = 95% → Server overload
👉 Application Issue
API response slow → Code or DB issue
👉 Network Issue
High latency → Slow communication between services

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Infra = System health 🖥️
 ✔ App = Performance 🚀
 ✔ Network = Connectivity 🌐
 ✔ All 3 together = Complete monitoring
